Description: renderer: never skip the output restore when resume finds no pause
 .
 meta_renderer_resume() guarded itself with g_return_if_fail (priv->is_paused).
 That is an early return, so a pause/resume imbalance did not merely log a
 warning -- it skipped klass->resume(), which on the native backend is what
 invalidates the onscreen framebuffers and brings KMS output back. The visible
 result is a session that logs in, holds the console, answers D-Bus, and renders
 nothing: a black screen indistinguishable from a hang, recoverable only by
 switching VT away and back to force a clean pause/resume cycle.
 .
 Seen on a machine running the GRD session-handover stack: after a day of remote
 sessions the console user logged in at the greeter, mutter resumed the existing
 session, the assertion tripped, and the screen stayed dark.
 .
 The two halves of resume are not equally risky. meta_renderer_native_resume()
 only calls meta_onscreen_native_invalidate() per view -- idempotent and cheap to
 repeat. clutter_frame_clock_uninhibit() is reference counted, so that is the one
 part worth skipping. Skip only that, and always restore the output.
 .
 This does not explain how the imbalance arises. It stops the imbalance from
 costing the user their display.
Author: Geoffrey <altarscn2@gmail.com>
Origin: downstream, GRD session-handover patch set
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-08-29

Index: mutter-50.1/src/backends/meta-renderer.c
===================================================================
--- mutter-50.1.orig/src/backends/meta-renderer.c
+++ mutter-50.1/src/backends/meta-renderer.c
@@ -346,19 +346,30 @@ meta_renderer_resume (MetaRenderer *rend
   MetaRendererClass *klass = META_RENDERER_GET_CLASS (renderer);
   GList *l;
 
-  g_return_if_fail (priv->is_paused);
-  priv->is_paused = FALSE;
-
-  for (l = priv->views; l; l = l->next)
+  if (priv->is_paused)
     {
-      ClutterStageView *stage_view = l->data;
-      ClutterFrameClock *frame_clock;
+      priv->is_paused = FALSE;
+
+      for (l = priv->views; l; l = l->next)
+        {
+          ClutterStageView *stage_view = l->data;
+          ClutterFrameClock *frame_clock;
 
-      if (meta_renderer_view_renders_offscreen (stage_view))
-        continue;
+          if (meta_renderer_view_renders_offscreen (stage_view))
+            continue;
 
-      frame_clock = clutter_stage_view_get_frame_clock (stage_view);
-      clutter_frame_clock_uninhibit (frame_clock);
+          frame_clock = clutter_stage_view_get_frame_clock (stage_view);
+          clutter_frame_clock_uninhibit (frame_clock);
+        }
+    }
+  else
+    {
+      /* No matching pause. The frame clocks were never inhibited and
+       * uninhibiting them would underflow their counters, so skip that -- but
+       * the output still has to come back. Returning here is what left a
+       * logged-in session holding the console with nothing on screen. */
+      g_warning ("Renderer resumed without a matching pause; "
+                 "restoring output anyway");
     }
 
   if (klass->resume)
